<title>JAPAN: Japan Jan imported vehicle sales up 4.1 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Jan imported vehicle sales up 4.1 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Domestic sales of imported vehicles in Japan rose 4.1 percent in January from a year earlier to 24,178 units, the Japan Automobile Importers' Association (JAIA) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It was the first gain in two months on a year-on-year basis and was the highest level ever for a January, surpassing the previous January record of 23,235 set last year.</p>
<p> Cars total		22,106  up    0.1 percent</p>
<p> - Cars over 2000 cc   14,167  down 10.5 percent</p>
<p> - Cars under 2000 cc   7,939  up   27.2 percent</p>
<p> Trucks total	     2,072  up   79.4 percent</p>
<p> Buses			  nil		    nil</p>
<p>January sales of vehicles produced by overseas units of Japanese makers totalled 4,200, down 35.3 percent from a year earlier.</p>
